  "scope": "Exact unchanged pinned Debian Firefox ESR ARM64, software/headless Wayland at 100 percent scale, ordinary wrapped native textareas. Zoom fallback/restoration is not native scaled support.",
  "implementation": {
    "provider": "Existing ordinary NSTextView/NSScrollView through the unchanged NativeUI wheel operation. No copied control, geometry, clamping, line/page/Shift behavior or shortcut table.",
    "hit_testing": "Use original nsIFrame hit info plus the existing eApzAwareListeners flag for owned native textareas, as the built-in range handler does. No dummy DOM listener or global APZ override.",
    "default": "Real EventStateManager post-DOM/default boundary retains page cancellation. Original default-handler PreventDefault acknowledges native consumption to APZ while preserving the content defaultPrevented getter.",
    "action": "Call original APZWheelActionFor; guarded exact-build Maybe::Some(Scroll) representation. Browser zoom/history preferences remain engine-owned.",
    "normalization": "Pixel distance is retained; GTK discrete wheel ticks use ten surface units per step, matching the native backend. AppKit owns resulting native movement.",
    "lifetime": "Retain semantic nodes across native/engine calls and revalidate node/control/frame identity before echoing native offsets through the original engine setter.",
    "focus": "Track the focus represented by the cached native bitmap. A retained display-list paint refreshes native focus/pixels on transition, without transferring engine scroll offsets or drawing a caret.",
    "recovery": "Existing viewport host-epoch restoration recreates the native object from retained live browser model. No input replay.",
    "fixture": "Browser-family-neutral real-seat reference fixture; private browser port checked before launch. Session logs write directly to evidence files so synchronous browser/native RPCs cannot fill a log pipe; Marionette close errors no longer skip owned-tree teardown.",
    "feature": "NEXTSPACE_FIREFOX_WHEEL=1 plus native multiline viewport, input/text/multiline flags, provider wheel capability and exact libxul build/instruction guards. Not installed as a desktop default."
  },
